    "created_at": "2017-04-07T18:49:00Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-04-07T18:49:00Z",
    "body": "SVG is a special case because `<iframe>` is an option (minus the bugs).  Of course, SVG is also a special case because all the sandbox attributes can be controlled by the browser.  \r\n\r\nHowever, even for Flash or PDF or other plug-in object, some of the sandbox restrictions (e.g., top-level navigation, pointer-lock, full-screen) could be enforced by the browser.  It seems strange not to have that option, except by nesting the `<object>` inside a sandboxed `<iframe>`.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
